[{:db/id -1, :adr/id "adr-2606039800-nusa-ritual-industrial-hemp-heritage-and-low-thc-cultivation", :adr/title "ADR-2606039800: nusa (幣) — ritual/industrial hemp heritage + low-THC cultivation Tier-B actor (R0)", :adr/status "proposed", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/source-format "edn", :adr/body "\n# ADR-2606039800: nusa (幣) — ritual/industrial hemp heritage + low-THC cultivation Tier-B actor (R0)\n\n**Status**: proposed\n**Date**: 2026-06-03\n**Deciders**: Jun Kawasaki\n\n# Context\n\nThe question that prompted this ADR: *「日本国内での大麻の解禁についての project / actor は設計されているか」*. A full search of the monorepo found **none** — no actor, ADR, lexicon, or cell whose subject is `cannabis` / `大麻` / `THC`. This ADR closes that gap, but **not** in the shape the word \"解禁\" usually implies. It does so along the only two lines that are charter-clean.\n\n## The cultural-history fact (true, and the load-bearing part)\n\nHemp (麻, *asa*) was deeply embedded in Japanese ritual life long before it was a drug-policy question:\n\n- **Shinto purification** — 注連縄 (*shimenawa*), 祓串 (*haraegushi*), the 大幣 (*ōnusa*) and 麻苧 (*asao*) fibre used in 祓 (*harae*) rites. Hemp was the fibre of *cleansing* — its ritual role is purification, not intoxication.\n- **Imperial accession (大嘗祭, Daijōsai)** — the 神御衣 offering comprises **麁服 (*aratae*, hemp cloth)** and **繒服 (*nigitae*, silk)**. The *aratae* is, by long tradition, woven from hemp cultivated and 調進 (presented) by the lineage of the **阿波忌部 (Awa Imbe)** clan — historically the 三木家 (Miki house) of 木屋平, Tokushima.\n- **Ise Jingū** distributes the 御札 known as **神宮大麻 (*Jingū-taima*)** — etymologically bound to *taima* / hemp.\n\nSo the claim \"hemp was culturally central, including imperial ritual\" is **historically correct**.\n\n## The honest correction (the line every gate rests on)\n\nThe traditional Japanese use of hemp was overwhelmingly **fibre and ritual purity**. Japanese landrace hemp was largely a **low-THC fibre type**; there is little documentary basis for a mainstream pre-modern *recreational/intoxicant* tradition. Therefore the narrative \"GHQ severed Japan's cannabis culture\" is half-right: what the occupation-era **大麻取締法 (Cannabis Control Act, 1948)** severed was principally **agricultural + ritual fibre cultivation**, not an intoxicant culture. Conflating \"hemp was central\" with \"recreational cannabis is traditional\" is the flaw that collapses the argument — and the boundary this actor encodes structurally.\n\n## The legal frame (now-open space vs still-prohibited)\n\nThe **2023 reform (令和5年法律第84号)** reorganized the regime — *primary sources (e-Gov 法令データ提供システム / 官報) must be cited by any cell; the figures below are `:representative` summary and require verification*:\n\n- 大麻取締法 was **renamed/restructured to 「大麻草の栽培の規制に関する法律」**;\n- **大麻由来医薬品** (e.g. CBD-based antiepileptics) became prescribable;\n- regulation shifted toward a **THC-content basis**, with a restructured **栽培者免許 (cultivator licence)** pathway for industrial/ritual low-THC hemp;\n- a new **使用罪** criminalized THC *use* (recreational intoxication remains prohibited).\n\nNet: **low-THC fibre + ritual cultivation + heritage = an institutionally OPEN space today**; **recreational THC = still prohibited**; **cannabis-derived medicine = a separate regulated lane (薬機法/医師法)**. These three lines map exactly onto nusa's gates.\n\n## Why an actor, and why this charter posture\n\netzhayyim's value system already incorporates 神道的 **祓い・清め** (Mission Charter §0/§1, ADR-2605192100). A heritage knowledge graph of ritual/industrial hemp and a design for licensed low-THC cultivation-revival sits squarely inside that, while staying clear of three constitutional tripwires: §1.13 Wellbecoming (no addictive/intoxicant design), §1.12 / G3 political-neutrality (no 解禁-推進/反対 lobbying — protects 1 SBT = 1 vote), and the §1.3 no-external-purchase / no-fiat-inflow rule (member-principal acquisition, ADR-2606012100). Direction 2 (legislative observation + public-comment support) is delivered by **extending** danjo (ADR-2605301600, G4 non-adjudicating) and moushibumi (ADR-2605312400, G3 neutral), reusing their existing constitutional machinery rather than minting new political logic.\n\n# Decision\n\nCreate **nusa (幣)** — a Tier-B religious-corp actor — and make two minimal, additive extensions to existing actors.\n\n## D1 — nusa actor (幣), DID `did:web:etzhayyim.com:actor:nusa`, status R0\n\nMandate (two faces, one ontology):\n\n1. **Heritage knowledge graph** — datafy the ritual/industrial hemp heritage (rites, artifacts, the Imbe lineage, low-THC cultivars and regions) into the **kotoba Datom log** (`:rite/* :imbe/* :hemp/*`) with `as-of` history (非終末論 — no final-state datom).\n2. **Low-THC cultivation-revival design** — model the *now-open* `栽培者免許` pathway for fibre/ritual hemp as a **member-principal, no-fiat-inflow, outward-gated** design (`:hemp.license/*`), and map ritual-artifact demand (注連縄/大幣) to licensed fibre supply.\n\nVocabulary: new `00-contracts/schemas/ritual-hemp-ontology.kotoba.edn`. The invariant `:hemp/thc-class ∈ {:fiber, :low-thc}` — `:psychoactive` is **not a representable value** (G1 enforcement point in schema, lexicon `const`, and `methods/analyze.py`).\n\n### Gates (immutable R0→R3)\n\n- **G1 low-THC / fibre-and-ritual-only** — only 繊維型 / 神事用 低THC 大麻草; recreational/high-THC excluded by construction (cultivar `:thc-class ∈ {:fiber,:low-thc}`).\n- **G2 non-recreational / 使用罪尊重** — never facilitates 嗜好使用; emits no consumption/dosing guidance.\n- **G3 non-adjudicating / political-neutral** — records cultural + legislative **facts** only; legal characterization routes to danjo/chigiri; takes **no 推進/反対 stance** on 解禁論.\n- **G4 member-principal / no-fiat-inflow** — `栽培者免許` fees never paid from religious-corp funds or a fiat processor (okaimono member-principal pattern, ADR-2606012100); nusa is never licensee-of-record / funder.\n- **G5 no-server-key** — cultivation/licence authorization = member signature; server signature refused (ADR-2605231525).\n- **G6 Murakumo-only** — all inference via LiteLLM `127.0.0.1:4000` (ADR-2605215000).\n- **G7 sourcing-honesty** — all seed `:representative`; legal/heritage figures flagged, primary-source-citing.\n- **G8 outward-gated** — real cultivation, live licence filing, live 法令/heritage ingest, atproto publish all Council Lv6+ + operator gated; R0 = offline design + intent only.\n- **G9 PII-consent** — cultivator personal data consent-bound + encrypted (`com.etzhayyim.encrypted.*`, ADR-2605181100).\n- **G10 medical boundary** — 大麻由来医薬品 is **out of scope** (薬機法/医師法 → yakushi/iyashi/mitate); nusa stops at fibre + ritual + heritage.\n\n### Non-goals\n\n- **N1** no recreational cannabis / THC intoxicant production or advocacy.\n- **N2** not a 解禁-推進/反対 political/lobbying organization (G3).\n- **N3** not a cannabis-derived-medicine manufacturer (→ yakushi).\n- **N4** never facilitates unlicensed cultivation.\n- **N5** no trafficking of high-THC seed/strains.\n\n### Cells (langgraph → WASM; Murakumo-only; `.solve()` raises `RuntimeError` at R0)\n\n`heritage_ingest` · `fiber_provenance` (coded reference; `ValueError` on psychoactive) · `cultivation_license_plan` · `rite_supply` · `observation_bridge` (thin router → danjo/chigiri; never adjudicates in-actor).\n\n### Lexicons (`com.etzhayyim.nusa.*`)\n\n`heritageRecord` · `hempCultivar` (`thcClass` const-gated, no `psychoactive`) · `ritualArtifact` · `cultivationLicensePlan` · `fiberProvenance`.\n\n## D2 — danjo extension (ADR-2605301600, non-adjudicating)\n\nAdd an open, versioned `methodNote` `cannabis-policy-legislative-trace` to `orgs/etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-danjo/methods/v1-jp-seed.json`: a **factual cross-reference** of 国会会議録 mentions + the 大麻取締法 → 大麻草の栽培の規制に関する法律 (令和5年法律第84号) statutory change. `nonAdjudicatingNotice=true`, mandatory `knownFalsePositiveModes`, severity = routing weight only (never a wrongdoing score). danjo finds + cites; it does not advocate.\n\n## D3 — moushibumi extension (ADR-2605312400, neutral)\n\nAdd neutral `participationTarget` entries to `orgs/etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-moushibumi/registry/targets.seed.json` for the 大麻草の栽培の規制に関する法律 関連 命令等 e-Gov 意見公募 (and optionally 国会請願). `verificationStatus: \"unverified-seed\"`; `notes` reaffirm **G3 political-neutrality** — no 推進/反対, no GOTV, open equally to citizens of either view.\n\n## D4 — registration\n\nRegister nusa in `00-contracts/schemas/actor-profile-seed.kotoba.edn` (`actors-v1` graph, ADR-2606013800), add a roster row to root `CLAUDE.md`, and register the ADR in `90-docs/adr/README.edn` + `deps.toml`. Worker `INFRA_ACTORS` reflection is a follow-up.\n\n# Consequences\n\n- The monorepo gains a charter-clean answer to the cannabis question that is **honest about the tradition** (fibre/ritual, not intoxicant) and **lands in the legally-open space** (low-THC cultivation + heritage), while structurally refusing the prohibited space.\n- danjo/moushibumi gain a worked example of cannabis-policy observation/participation without any new political logic.\n- R0 is design-only; nothing cultivates, files, or publishes outward without Council Lv6+ + operator (G8).\n- The `:hemp/thc-class` invariant means the data model itself cannot express a recreational-cannabis catalog — the prohibition is enforced by construction, not policy.\n\n# Alternatives Considered\n\n- **A recreational-cannabis legalization-advocacy actor** — **rejected**. Violates G3/§1.12 (political-neutrality, protects 1 SBT = 1 vote), sits in tension with §1.13 Wellbecoming, and would have nusa take sides in 解禁論. Lobbying-for-a-position is constitutionally unavailable.\n- **A cannabis-derived-medicine actor** — **deferred/rejected for nusa**. That is 薬機法/医師法 territory belonging to yakushi/iyashi/mitate; folding it in would blur the medical-device/UPL boundaries those actors carefully hold.\n- **A single new actor that also owns the legislative-observation + public-comment cells** — **rejected**. It would duplicate danjo's G4 non-adjudicating and moushibumi's G3 neutral machinery and scatter the political-neutrality guarantee. Extending the existing actors is minimal and keeps one home for each invariant.\n\n# References\n\n- ADR-2605192100 — Mission Charter (§0 祓い・清め, §1.12 Transparent Force / 1 SBT = 1 vote, §1.13 Wellbecoming)\n- ADR-2605192200 — Charter Compliance Rider v2.0\n- ADR-2605301600 — danjo (public-accountability oversight, G4 non-adjudicating)\n- ADR-2605312400 — moushibumi (democratic-participation concierge, G3 neutral)\n- ADR-2605250500 — yakushi (pharmaceutical R&D; medical boundary)\n- ADR-2605262700 — chigiri (legal-procedure substrate; UPL boundary)\n- ADR-2606012100 — okaimono (member-principal assisted-checkout; no-fiat-inflow pattern)\n- ADR-2605215000 — Murakumo-only inference\n- ADR-2606013800 — actor profile + dynamic did.json (actors-v1 registration)\n- ADR-2605181100 — encrypted envelope (`com.etzhayyim.encrypted.*`)\n- Primary legal sources (to be cited by cells, not yet ingested): e-Gov 法令データ提供システム — 大麻草の栽培の規制に関する法律; 官報 令和5年法律第84号\n", :adr/path "90-docs/adr/2606039800-nusa-ritual-industrial-hemp-heritage-and-low-thc-cultivation-tier-b-actor-r0.edn", :adr/source-repo "root", :adr/topic "nusa-ritual-industrial-hemp-heritage", :adr/last_verified "2026-06-03", :adr/date "2026-06-03", :adr/authoritative true, :adr/related ["2605301600" "2605312400" "2605250500" "2605262700" "2606012100" "2606011500"], :adr/authoritative_for ["nusa-actor" "ritual-hemp-ontology"]}]
